(1369,2874,'Hemorrhage into the peritoneal cavity.','en',2,'2026-06-24 20:08:26',NULL,NULL,'4207FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1370,2875,'Union of the fragments of a fractured bone in a faulty or abnormal position. If two bones parallel to one another unite by osseous tissue, the result is a crossunion. (From Manual of Orthopaedic Terminology, 4th ed)','en',2,'2026-06-24 20:08:26',NULL,NULL,'4206FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1371,2876,'A fracture in which union fails to occur, the ends of the bone becoming rounded and eburnated, and a false joint occurs. (Stedman, 25th ed)','en',2,'2026-06-24 20:08:26',NULL,NULL,'4205FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1372,2880,'Involuntary movements of the eye that are divided into two types, jerk and pendular. Jerk nystagmus has a slow phase in one direction followed by a corrective fast phase in the opposite direction, and is usually caused by central or peripheral vestibular dysfunction. Pendular nystagmus features oscillations that are of equal velocity in both directions and this condition is often associated with visual loss early in life. (Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p272)','en',2,'2026-06-24 20:08:26',NULL,NULL,'4196FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
